# NestJS Backend Rules

## Architecture
- Feature-sliced: each feature has main + shared libs
- Thin app modules: only import feature main modules + health
- Bootstrap via bootstrapNestApi() from shared lib
- Fastify adapter for all apps
- Health endpoints: /live, /ready on all apps

## Patterns
- Port/Adapter: use InMemory* for dev, Postgres* for prod
- Global validation pipe: transform, whitelist, forbidNonWhitelisted
- RFC 9457 error responses via ClientDataValidationException
- Authentication guards: SessionAuthGuard plus database-backed RBAC guards
- DTOs with class-validator decorators
- Use @Public() to mark unauthenticated routes

## Database
- MikroORM with PostgreSQL
- Migrations via pnpm db:migrate
- POSTGRES_SYNCHRONIZE=false (never auto-sync schema)
- Separate migration job runs before app deployment

## Security
- Rate limiting: 100 req/min, Redis-backed in production
- Helmet for security headers
- CORS origins configured per environment
- No in-memory persistence in production
- PBKDF2-SHA256 with 120k iterations for passwords
